  "narrative": "3.131(d)\nSanitation.\nNumerous field mice were observed scurrying around the enclosure housing the prehensile-tailed porcupine and\ntortoises. The mice were observed climbing the branches, taking food from the food bowl, and returning to the center of\nthe artificial tree and through the roots under the tree. These mice could contaminate the porcupine's food with their urine\nand feces and bring unwanted disease and other vermin.\nFacility must determine areas of entrance and effectively remove these mice to protect the prehensile tailed porcupine.\nA safe and effective program for the control of insects, ectoparasites, and avian and mammalian pests shall be\nestablished and maintained.\nTO BE CORRECTED BY: NOVEMBER 17, 2026\nThis inspection and exit briefing were conducted with the facility representatives.\nYou may appeal all or part of any inspection report by submitting a written statement contesting the findings\u2014along with\nany supporting documentation\u2014to the Deputy Administrator. Appeals of routine, focused, or attempted inspections must\nbe received within 21 days of report issuance as shown by the signature line of this report.\nAppeals may be sent by email to AnimalCare@usda.gov.\nAppeals sent by mail should be addressed to:\nDeputy Administrator\nAPHIS Animal Care (AC)\nU.S. Department of Agriculture\n2150 Centre Avenue, Building B\nMailstop #3W11\nFort Collins, CO 80526-8117\n\nn",
